prompt:
Create a labeled material reference sheet matching the attached approved ultra minimal pixel art item style. Use case stylized-concept. Each item must look authored on a tiny 16x16 pixel grid enlarged with hard nearest-neighbor square pixels. No intricate detail, no antialiasing, no gradient or smooth glow, 3-5 flat colors per item. Flat opaque charcoal background. Large readable simple labels under sprites. Title "MATERIALS". A clean 4 columns x 4 rows grid with exactly 16 samples, SAME simple diagonal sword silhouette and SAME brown grip in every cell, only blade/main material changes. This is a cosmetic material comparison, not a valid loot chart. Follow this exact row-major order and labels:
Bone: ivory with one tan pixel;
Steel: medium cool gray with white edge;
Iron: dark slate gray with muted edge;
Bronze: copper brown with pale tan edge;
Gold: warm yellow with ochre shade;
Mithril: pale ice blue with cyan shade;
Glass: pale cyan outline with dark background-colored center implying transparency;
Obsidian: near black plum with purple edge;
Shadow: deep indigo with TWO detached dark violet square pixels at blade tip;
Willow: warm wood brown blade with ONE green pixel by guard;
Silver: almost white with neutral gray shade, distinct from blue mithril;
Crystal: lavender with pale violet edge;
Stone: muted taupe gray with ONE darker chip pixel;
Unknown: desaturated gray with one mismatched pale square embedded in blade;
Strange: muted teal blade with two coral pixels;
Celestial: pale warm cream blade with TWO gold square star pixels near tip.
Keep silhouette approximately 12-14 logical pixels long, blade only 2-3 pixels wide. Each sprite must have big countable square pixels and extreme simplicity just like approved reference. No decorative frame, no other illustrations, no material spheres, no characters, no realistic texture. Label every material clearly.
